{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"The startup probe confirms a socket leak on malformed persisted heads: one bind, zero socket closes, and one local-store close. An oversized `--dht-follow` port also escapes `startup` as a raw `NumberFormatException`.\n\nThe kill tests use close-and-reopen rather than process termination. The process test’s first-contact assertion also races installation: it starts the reader against an already populated board and waits for a VM switch before typing `require`."}}
