{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-06 08:02:55 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-06 15:02:55 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: 01a1103a-2d0e-7f82-b9a3-8f50d00edd21\n\n- **P1 | src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc:274 |** `dht/join` binds before persisted heads are validated. If restoration refuses, the catch closes only `base`, leaving the node’s socket open. Focused JVM seam evaluation with truncated heads returned a refusal with `bound=1`, `socket-closed=0`, `local-closed=1`. **Concrete fix:** validate before binding, or close the joined node on every subsequent startup failure; assert socket cleanup in refusal tests.\n\n- **P1 | src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:121 |** An overflowing decimal port escapes startup as an exception. JVM evaluation of `--dht-follow <64-hex>@127.0.0.1:9999999999999999999999999999` threw `NumberFormatException`, because `parse-int` uses `Long/parseLong` and startup rethrows errors without `ex-data`. **Concrete fix:** make numeric parsing total on JVM and Dart, returning a designed refusal for overflow; test oversized ports through `startup` and `dht join`.\n\n- **P2 | src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc:109 |** The EDN reader accepts only the first form without checking the remainder. Both `{:version 1 :heads {}} {:broken` and `{:version 1 :heads {}} garbage` returned successful empty records in JVM probes. **Concrete fix:** require exactly one complete EDN record followed by EOF, allowing only normal whitespace/comments; test trailing forms and truncated suffixes.\n\n- **P2 | src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc:136 |** File reading has neither a byte bound nor strict UTF-8 validation on JVM/Node. A JVM probe decoded an invalid `0xff` byte in a comment as `�`, and parsing accepted the file. Oversized comment padding is likewise accepted and read wholly into memory. **Concrete fix:** use a bounded byte read and strict UTF-8 decoding, returning named refusals for invalid encoding and excessive size on every host.\n\n- **P2 | src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc:530 |** Refusal-ring overflow permanently suppresses diagnostics. After appending 65 notes to the 64-entry ring, two `step-board` calls returned no lines and retained the original cursor; `next` kept answering `:dao.stream/gap`. **Concrete fix:** adopt the gap’s recovery cursor, report lost notes, and drain retained entries. Add an overflow test that also checks subsequent refusals remain visible.\n\n- **P2 | test/yin/repl/dht_head_test.cljc:487 |** H3’s required process-kill cases remain untested. Both cases explicitly close and reopen the shell, so they cannot establish recovery without graceful cleanup or recovery with a stale temp file. **Concrete fix:** synchronize child processes at the two persistence barriers, kill without cleanup, and verify old/new-head recovery and lock release.\n\n- **P2 | test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj:1044 |** The first-contact assertion races head installation. The publisher already holds a head before readers start, and the helper waits for a VM-switch response before typing the first `require`. Installation can therefore precede that require, making the required pending-line assertion fail despite correct behavior. **Concrete fix:** hold publication until the reader demonstrably parks, then publish and assert completion without further input.\n\nNo files edited; verified suites were not repeated. No additional actionable findings in host-module rule placement, node-state persistence, docs/help, or apply/rpc separation.\n\nBlocked on the findings above, Node and Dart lanes passing, and Architect sign-off."}}
